  "title": "Concentric Circle Stitch: Rectangle, round 6",
  "description": "PE-DESIGN 11.50's Concentric Circle Stitch, round 6: circles about the centre one row apart. With the start point on a whole circle the whole circles go first, outside in, then the cut ones after a trim; with the start point beyond the whole circles (portrait shapes, a triangle's corner) PE starts there on the cut circles and works inwards to the middle. PE: starts at the bottom middle (0,+20.0) running left and ends at the centre: the cut circles first, outside in. The seam is not compared.",
